# Programmatic Asset Generation

## Context
- This game generates all UI elements, icons, and sprites programmatically at runtime
- No external image files are used for game entities or UI components
- All visual elements are created using Phaser's graphics primitives

## Requirements
- Use GraphicsGenerator methods to create textures at runtime
- Never attempt to load UI or game entity images as external assets
- Call generateUIAssets() in the Preloader scene
- Generate all textures before they are needed by game objects
- Use Phaser's graphics primitives for UI elements

## Examples
<example>
// Generate all UI assets in Preloader
preload() {
  // Generate all UI assets programmatically
  this.graphicsGenerator.generateUIAssets();
  this.graphicsGenerator.generatePlayerTexture();
  this.graphicsGenerator.generateEnemyTexture();
}
</example>

<example type="invalid">
// Don't load non-existent image files
preload() {
  // This is incorrect - files don't exist
  this.load.image("button", "assets/ui/button.png");
  this.load.image("health_bar", "assets/ui/health_bar.png");
}
</example>

## Common GraphicsGenerator Methods
- `generatePlayerTexture()` - Creates player character sprites
- `generateEnemyTexture()` - Creates enemy sprites
- `generateTowerTexture()` - Creates tower defense structures
- `setupParticleEffects()` - Creates particle effects for various game events

## Benefits
- Reduced asset loading time
- Smaller game file size
- Easier to make visual changes without requiring new art assets
- Consistent appearance across different devices and resolutions
- Avoids issues with missing image files 